{"edits": [{"finding_ids": ["app/api_errors.py:10:validator"], "search": "MESSAGE_CODES = {
    "field required": "MISSING",
    "value is not a valid integer": "NOT_AN_INTEGER",
    "ensure this value has at least": "TOO_SHORT",
}", "replace": "# Pydantic v2 messages are different, so key on the stable error `type` instead.
MESSAGE_CODES = {
    "missing": "MISSING",
    "int_parsing": "NOT_AN_INTEGER",
    "int_type": "NOT_AN_INTEGER",
    "string_too_short": "TOO_SHORT",
}", "explanation": "Pydantic v2 reworded error messages (e.g. 'Field required'), so message-prefix matching no longer works. Match on the stable v2 error `type` values instead."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/api_errors.py:10:validator"], "search": "            code = next((c for m, c in MESSAGE_CODES.items() if err["msg"].startswith(m)), "INVALID")", "replace": "            code = MESSAGE_CODES.get(err["type"], "INVALID")", "explanation": "Look up the code by v2 error type rather than by the message text."}], "notes": "The validator migration to @field_validator + @classmethod was already correct and is left alone. The test failure came from error-message matching: v2 messages changed ('Field required', 'Input should be a valid integer...', 'String should have at least...'), so every error fell through to INVALID. The fix maps v2 error types (missing, int_parsing, string_too_short) to the public codes. I also added int_type, which v2 raises for non-str/number inputs like None."}
